+# Bounded production proposal, Request033
+
+This is a reviewable proposal, not production authority. No production helper, renewal, stop, capture, transfer, signing import, install or resume has run. Both production refusals and all21 null evidence slots remain unchanged. Exact identities, paths, capacity floors and deadlines are in production-contract.json; the delivery's manifest SHA binds the immutable executable source without a circular self-hash.
+
+The executor remains development-only. Review must not confuse a unit template with an enabled production controller. External consumer and CA calls in the mapping tests are explicit fixtures; live successor consumer acceptance and CA issuance remain separate gates. The proposal requires those acceptance results before operational enrollment, not a speculative assumption that a green fixture covered them.
+
+1. Before any separately authorized start, refresh read-only inventory, both application-role writer census, installed source hashes, exact container/image/config, machine and mount UUIDs, controls, private destination ownership and available capacity. Recheck expiry: the last metadata observation was 2026-09-22T00:12:55Z, expiry2026-09-22T20:53:07Z. No new admission after2026-09-22T18:00:00Z under this packet. Changed sources/identities or expired authority stop the procedure. A revised window requires a fresh proposal.
+2. Keep the existing Mac scheduler mutex continuously owned through the common durable journal. Record intent before any helper/login/remote effect. Reconcile the retained Request029 pointer and Request032 disposition by authenticated readback; never clear or migrate them. Disable obsolete VM101 intake as already recorded, keep its WebUI stopped, preserve unrelated VM101 services. Preserve processing pause, attention, checkpoint and boot reconciliation, and never invoke checkpoint acknowledgement as a capture side effect.
+3. Provision only the separately approved root-owned0700 control/source paths and verify the sealed member hashes. Existing production boot pause remains authoritative. A Docker drop-in orders that pause before unless-stopped serving startup. After Docker, an exact-incumbent recovery service controls management admission; the existing paused cron status path remains. No global cron stop or unrelated Docker restart is proposed. Because Docker can restore serving before management admission, processing pause must exist first. Tested transient ordering is not a reboot test. Actual reboot proof needs a later approved disruptive test.
+4. For a separately approved capture, scope CONNECT control only to community_brain_prod and cbm_prod_runtime/cbm_prod_migration on shared DB10.1.10.50. Reject unknown application administrators instead of killing them; do not alter unrelated roles/databases. Stop only the pinned serving incumbent if required for filesystem consistency. Capture within120 seconds; independent root finalizer restores original CONNECT ACLs and the exact unchanged incumbent by180 seconds even when Mac/SSH dies. Failed recovery closes admission and leaves a durable incident. Deadlines assume reachable control storage, Docker and DB, not unconditional availability.
+5. Capture the exact12 components: native database dump; VM109 files, config, corpus, meeting-archive-20260910, automation, automation-public, manual-approvals and the complete private /etc/community-brain-production runtime-config tree; dormant VM101 open-webui-data volume; its original /app/backend/.webui_secret_key outside that volume; Mac private management/ownership journals needed for recovery. Do not substitute public projections for private state, regenerate embeddings, replay unknown operations, or acknowledge checkpoints. Bind source and destination manifests and before/after stable inventories; a changing source aborts. Preserve uid/gid/mode/mtime, empty directories and contained relative links (46 observed in WebUI). Refuse xattrs/ACLs/hardlinks/special/privileged files and absolute, broken or escaping symlinks. Current scans found none of those unsupported forms.
+6. Use the exclusive PBS-host path in production-contract.json, outside its datastore, root0700; parent belongs to backup uid34 and is not chmodded. Require at least20GiB free (445140434944 bytes observed). No encryption or scheduled-backup coverage is implied. Restore privately on VM109 under the separate exclusive private-restore path, also root0700 with20GiB minimum (61381419008 bytes observed). This supersedes the unauthorized VM108 private enclave. PBS has no Postgres/Docker runtime and is a copy destination only. VM109's restore PostgreSQL must have a distinct system identifier from source DB10.1.10.50, network none, no published ports or production mounts. This is independent from the source DB server, not independent from VM109 hardware failure.
+7. Preserve all original, partial, failed and replacement objects indefinitely pending explicit deletion review. Exclusive capture ID is cbm-private-review-20260922-033; an existing directory is never overwritten or adopted. The17-byte signing file must match7638e389c27761152e8c894b9fff5b328e78964225e51c9514f3273dde931ef5, including any trailing bytes; retain its0644 mode inside the private0700 envelope. No key generation/normalization is a preservation substitute.
+8. Restore unchanged serving before the180-second deadline; allow offline comparison up to1800 seconds without extending the outage. Compare actual schema/ACL/default-ACL/roles, all10 canonical tables,19 indexes, zero sequences, Alembic, relationships, outcome_unknown records, model-call response hashes, operations/rejected-events, filesystem manifests, vector/FTS identity and WebUI SQLite/Chroma/uploads/signing identity. A failed comparison retains all evidence and original rollback state.
+9. Only a later separately authorized acceptance phase can prove real sessions/browser behavior with the original key, successor WebUI/API/collector/Kuma/Prometheus credential acceptance, current CA issuance/deployment and negative old/cross-scope credentials, vector/FTS equivalence, capacity under the real workload, protected off-host receipt, persistent installation and reboot recovery. Processing resume, cutover and provider spending remain separate decisions. None is inferred from this packet.
+
+Rollback owner: home.servers, with an independent VM109 root systemd finalizer bound to the exact incumbent and source, not the interactive Mac process. Original image/container, private data, signing bytes, old source and held jobs remain retained. No resize, shared-service restart or replacement of unrelated infrastructure is included.
